From: wh1ter0se69 <62149665+wh1ter0se69@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:18:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] GeneralsX FF: sub-allocate the fixed-function VS
 constants instead of renaming the buffer per upload

UpdateFixedFunctionVS called m_vsFixedFunction.AllocSlice() for every upload - a new buffer storage from
DxvkMemoryAllocator (under its mutex) plus an invalidateBuffer on the CS thread - and an upload happens on nearly
every draw that sets its own world matrix. On a zoomed-out 6v6 (~17k such draws a frame, Mac Mini, macOS sample of
the main thread) that mutex was contended: ~2/3 of UpdateFixedFunctionVS was std::mutex lock/unlock with a kernel
wait/wake inside DxvkMemoryAllocator::allocateMemory.

Stream them like the programmable VS constants already are (UploadConstantSet): a 1 MB buffer, Alloc() per upload,
one storage per ~500 uploads and a bindUniformBufferRange per upload. Upstream DXVK 3.0 streams these constants the
same way (GetConstantBuffer(CbvIndex::VSFixedFunction).AllocTyped). No shader, key or binding-layout change; the
bytes written are the same.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YLkLUnAQgjdzMvcL22pmru
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
index 4313f6a4..483797cc 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -5810,10 +5810,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
       DxsoConstantBuffers::VSClipPlanes,
       caps::MaxClipPlanes * sizeof(D3D9ClipPlane));
 
+    // GeneralsX FF: streamed like the programmable VS constants above (Alloc per upload from a 1 MB buffer), not
+    // renamed per upload - see UpdateFixedFunctionVS.
     m_vsFixedFunction = D3D9ConstantBuffer(this,
       DxsoProgramType::VertexShader,
       DxsoConstantBuffers::VSFixedFunction,
-      sizeof(D3D9FixedFunctionVS));
+      DefaultConstantBufferSize);
 
     m_psFixedFunction = D3D9ConstantBuffer(this,
       DxsoProgramType::PixelShader,
@@ -7901,7 +7903,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
     if (m_flags.test(D3D9DeviceFlag::DirtyFFVertexData)) {
       m_flags.clr(D3D9DeviceFlag::DirtyFFVertexData);
 
-      auto mapPtr = m_vsFixedFunction.AllocSlice();
+      // GeneralsX FF: sub-allocate, never AllocSlice. AllocSlice took a NEW buffer storage from DxvkMemoryAllocator for
+      // every upload, i.e. for nearly every draw that sets its own world matrix; on a zoomed-out 6v6 (~17k such draws a
+      // frame) that allocator mutex was contended and ~2/3 of this function's time (Mini profile, 02/10/2026). Alloc
+      // takes one storage per ~500 uploads and binds a range, as UploadConstantSet already does; upstream 3.0 does the
+      // same for these constants. The bytes written are unchanged.
+      auto mapPtr = m_vsFixedFunction.Alloc(sizeof(D3D9FixedFunctionVS));
 
       auto WorldView    = m_state.transforms[GetTransformIndex(D3DTS_VIEW)] * m_state.transforms[GetTransformIndex(D3DTS_WORLD)];
       auto NormalMatrix = inverse(WorldView);
